    "full_name": "badawytpu-ux/summer-practice-geant4",
    "url": "https://github.com/badawytpu-ux/summer-practice-geant4",
    "description": "Geant4 simulations for summer practice: proton Bragg peak and Pb-Al PET converter",
    "stars": 0,
    "language": "C++",
    "updated_at": "2026-08-02T16:36:16Z",
    "license": null,
    "topics": [],
    "readme_excerpt": "# Summer Practice — Geant4 (2026)\n\nMonte Carlo simulations written during the summer practice at JINR (Dubna) using **Geant4**.\nTwo studies: the proton **Bragg peak** in a water phantom, and optimization of a two-layer\n**Pb–Al converter** for a gas PET detector (511 keV gammas).\n\nAuthor: Гад Таха Махмуд Бадави, group 0А31, Инженерная школа ядерных технологий, ТПУ.\n\n## Projects\n\n### Cube / Cube2 — proton Bragg peak\nWater phantom 350×350×350 mm³, protons of 230 MeV (and 60–220 MeV).\n- `watercube.cc` — main program (`int main()`).\n- `DetectorConstruction.*` — phantom geometry (`G4_WATER`).\n- `PrimaryGeneratorAction.*` — 230 MeV proton source.\n- `PhysicsList`, `TrackerSD`, `TrackerHit` — physics and scoring.\n\nCube2 additionally contains the analysis programs (pure C++/ROOT):\n- `task2_fit_all_energies_quadratic.cpp` — piecewise-quadratic approximation of the Bragg curves.\n- `task3_parameterization.cpp` — energy parameterization R(E), Dmax(E) for arbitrary energy.\n\n### PETConverter_clean — Pb–Al converter\nTwo-layer Pb + Al converter for 511 keV gammas; records electrons leaving the Al layer.\n- `PETConverter.cc` — main program (`int main()`).\n- `src/DetectorConstruction.cc` — Pb and Al layers, thicknesses, electron scoring layer.\n- `src/PrimaryGammaGeneratorAction.cc` — 511 keV gamma source.\n- `src/TrackerSD.cc` — logs exit coordinates, kinetic energy, exit angle, radial displacement.\n- `src/ElectronExitRunAction.cc` — converter efficiency (N_e / N_gamma).\n- `analysis/` — ROOT programs for the Al/Pb thickness scans and result plots.\n- `macros/` — run and scan macros.\n\n## Build\n\n```bash\ncd PETConverter_clean\nmkdir build && cd build\ncmake ..\nmake\n./PETConverter run.mac\n```\n\nThe Cube/Cube2 phantom projects build the same way (Geant4 + CMake). The `task*.cpp`\nanalysis programs are standalone: `g++ task2_fit_all_energies_quadratic.cpp -o task2`.\n",
